[[b]]Consolidation playbook — change {{CHANGE_ID}}[[/b]][[g]] — agent-executed (ADR 0005); the spec shrinks, the behaviour does not change.[[/g]]

Capability: [[c]]{{CAPABILITY}}[[/c]] — {{SHAPE}}

Execute in order, in a single linear pass:

1. Read the spec and its history:
       [[c]]doctrina context {{CAPABILITY}} --concat[[/c]]
       [[c]]doctrina why {{CAPABILITY}}[[/c]]
2. Find what the spec says more than once: a requirement a later one
   superseded, two requirements stating the same rule, a criterion proven
   by another one, a bullet describing behaviour that no longer exists.
   You decide; the CLI only measures. Keep every rule the code still
   honours — consolidating removes words, never guarantees.
3. Write the delta with the ops (the scaffold is at
   .doctrina/changes/{{CHANGE_ID}}/specs/{{CAPABILITY}}/delta.md):
       [[c]]doctrina change delta {{CHANGE_ID}} {{CAPABILITY}} --op "remove-requirement <section> <n>: <why>"[[/c]]
       [[c]]doctrina change delta {{CHANGE_ID}} {{CAPABILITY}} --op "replace-requirement <section> <n>: <merged text>"[[/c]]
       [[c]]doctrina change delta {{CHANGE_ID}} {{CAPABILITY}} --op "remove-criterion <n>: <why>"[[/c]]
       [[c]]doctrina change delta {{CHANGE_ID}} {{CAPABILITY}} --bump minor[[/c]]
[[g]]   Ops run in order and a removal renumbers what follows it: write the[[/g]]
[[g]]   removals of one section highest number first. Every kept criterion[[/g]]
[[g]]   must still cite proof that exists — coverage gates the close.[[/g]]
[[g]]   Preview the merged spec: [[/g]][[c]]doctrina change check {{CHANGE_ID}} --verbose[[/c]]
4. Fill the proposal's What (what was merged or removed, and why each) and
   replace the placeholder tasks; no code changes.
5. Close in one attested pass:
       [[c]]doctrina close {{CHANGE_ID}}[[/c]]
